  📋 SIGNAL (all required, on the latest daily candle)
  RSI = Wilder RSI(14); RSI average = 9-day simple average of RSI.

  1) RSI crossed ABOVE its average 3-10 trading days ago.
  2) RSI then rose at least 3.0 points above its average.
  3) RSI pulled back to within 1.5 points of its average (never more
     than 2.0 points below it since the cross).
  4) That touch was in the last 2 days and TODAY RSI is rising,
     above its average and moving away from it.

  📋 OUTPUT (reasonable defaults — not explicitly requested)
  Entry_Price = today's CLOSE
  Stop_Loss   = lowest LOW of the pullback (from RSI's peak to today)
  SMA50       = trend context (score bonus only, not a gate)
